    ":question/id": "2e9f1022-1926-5a16-afea-9527e06c53ee",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-22798",
    ":question/problem": "If ${b}^{9}=x$ and ${b}^{2}=y$, what is the value of $\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we carry out the substitution\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}=\\frac{{({b}^{9})}^{3}}{{b}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply power rule followed by the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{({b}^{9})}^{3}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{b}^{9\\cdot 3}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{b}^{27}}{{b}^{2}} & = \\\\ {b}^{27-2} & = \\\\ {b}^{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
