    ":question/id": "3b874545-de9e-5368-9969-5a0f4efc79db",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-34432",
    ":question/problem": "If $\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{-6/5}}={z}^{k},$ then $k=$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express the radical as a fractional power and then we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{-6/5}} & = \\\\ {({z}^{-6/5})}^{1/3} & = \\\\ {z}^{(-6/5)(1/3)} & = \\\\ {z}^{-2/5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"
